          "file": "src/billing/status.ts",
          "claim": "WHAT: Propagating NotReadyError from fetchStatus activates pollCharge's resubmit path for a charge the gateway already holds. WHY: Because gw.submit is documented as non-idempotent, this can create duplicate charges whenever a charge is accepted but pending settlement. HOW: Reconcile the NotReadyError contract between errors.ts and poller.ts; if NotReadyError means the gateway already has the charge, change pollCharge to retry/repoll instead of calling gw.submit.",
          "keep": true,
          "rationale": "The evidence supports the finding. In errors.ts, NotReadyError is documented as 'The gateway has the charge but has not settled it yet (transient),' while in poller.ts the same error is interpreted as 'the gateway never received it' and triggers an unconditional `gw.submit(charge.payload)` resubmit. fetchStatus now propagates NotReadyError unchanged, so pollCharge will indeed resubmit a charge the gateway already holds. This contract mismatch creates a real duplicate-charge risk whenever `gw.submit` is non-idempotent. The previous review decision addressed the opposite failure (NotReadyError being converted to a terminal FailedError, preventing any retry), not the duplicate-submission failure described here, so this is a distinct problem and not a repeat.",
